  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 5-15 EUR during the initial 10-15 day forecast horizon, failing to anticipate the sharp drop from ~79 EUR to ~67 EUR.",
    "Adjust for momentum lag: The model exhibits a significant lag in reacting to trend reversals, predicting a slow, linear recovery while the true market experiences a V-shaped recovery (sharp drop followed by rapid rebound) starting around day 15.",
    "Incorporate sentiment volatility: Positive sentiment spikes (0.20-0.33) in the history do not trigger immediate upward price corrections in the model; the model must be weighted to react more aggressively to sentiment shifts rather than relying on historical price smoothing.",
    "Cap mean reversion speed: The model assumes a gradual mean reversion to ~76 EUR; correction rules must accelerate the projected recovery rate to match the observed rapid climb back to 80 EUR in the final forecast days.",
    "Reduce overshoot on recovery: The model's linear projection fails to capture the volatility of the recovery phase; apply a non-linear adjustment to increase forecast variance during the rebound period."
